{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/490936-the-purely-speculative-and-for-fun-thread-about-2ed-kith-ideas","id":490936,"title":"The Purely Speculative And For Fun Thread About 2ed Kith Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-24T14:40:29-07:00","id":490936,"title":"The Purely Speculative And For Fun Thread About 2ed Kith Ideas","content":"Because using your imagination is fun. I came up with 6 Kiths and examples for each Kith under the Seemings. You are completely free to subvert the archetypal notion of each Kith or switch them around.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Hero: </span>your Keeper gave you the dubious honor of being the main face in one its many schemes and theaters. Your blessing is &quot;Brave To The End&quot;: you gain a +3 bonus to all rolls for resisting fear, and when your Health is full of lethal damage, it does not bleed over into aggravated until the end of the scene. Any Hero may go down a bad road in life and become a villain, sometimes believing he is the Hero of anther story.</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fairest Hero: Knight In Shining Armor. Darkling Hero: Cunning Rogue. Ogre Hero: Boisterous Gladiator. Elemental Hero: Explorer Of The Strange And Extreme. Beast Hero: Predator Other Predators Fear. Wizened Hero: Gadget Genius.</span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Royal:</span> you were given a position of great authority, second only to your Keeper's. Your blessing is the &quot;Command Of Nobility&quot;: you receive a +3 bonus to all rolls for maintaining peace and order, and when you need to make an important announcement to the Kingdom, be it to celebrate a victory or prepare for battle, you gain a +5 bonus. You needn't be the actual ruler, but yout will benefit from this blessing as long as you act within the interests of Rulership.</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fairest Royal: Prim And Proper Aristocrat. Ogre Royal: Warlord. Darkling Royal: Machiavellian (in the correct meaning of the word). Elemental Royal: Impartial Adviser. Beast Royal: Intuitive Enforcer<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">. Wizened Royal: Thinker Ahead.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Witch/Wizard: <span style=\"font-size:12px\">you were given or stole a fraction of your Keeper's magical affinity, and now you lay curses and bring blessing as you see fit. Your blessing is &quot;Double, Double, Toil And Trouble&quot;: you gain a +3 bonus to all rolls involving goblin fruit/oddments and +3 to Contracts that strengthen or weaken, but don't cause physical damage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Fairest Witch: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Fairy_with_Turquoise_Hair\" target=\"_blank\">Fairy With Turquoise Hair</a>. Darkling Witch: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morgan_le_Fay\" target=\"_blank\">Morgana Le Fey</a>. Ogre Witch: Baba Yaga. Elemental Witch: Spriggan. Beast Witch: Nordic Crow, Western Goat and Eastern Fox. Wizened Witch: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hag\" target=\"_blank\">Hag</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Artificer: </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">you built everything from swords and shields to castles and statues for your Keeper. Your blessing is &quot;Wonder Worker&quot;: you gain +3 on all rolls involving the building, repairing, improving and even dismantling of mundane objects, and +2 for Hedgespinning.</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Fairest Artificer: Aesthetics Aficionado. Darkling Artificer: Trap Master. Ogre Artificer: Efficiency Over Looks. Elemental Artificer: Golem Sculptor. Beast Artificer: Hearth Weaver. Wizened Artificer: Wyrd Scientist.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Creature: <span style=\"font-size:12px\">you were turned into any type of monster from myth and legend alike. Your blessing is &quot;Claws And Fangs&quot;: you gain a +1L damage bonus and Armor Piercing 2 on Brawl rolls. These natural weapons don't have to be actual claws and teeth, they can be a burning touch, rock hard fists and so on. Dragons are a special case: they can fit into any Seeming, such as Ogre for European Dragons and Elemental for Chinese Dragons.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Fairest Creature: Unicorn, Angel, Mermaid, Succubus, Nymph. Satyr. Darkling Creature: Ghosts, Ghoulies And Creepy Crawlies. Ogre Creature: Troll, Minotaur, Giant and <a href=\"http://&#91;/SIZE\" target=\"_blank\">Oni</a>. Elemental Creature: Balrog, <a href=\"http://&#91;/SIZE\" target=\"_blank\">Tsukumogami</a>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elemental#Paracelsus\" target=\"_blank\">Gnome, Undine, Salamander and Sylph.</a> Beast Creature: Hydra, Manticore, Centaur, Griffon. Wizened Creature: pixies, goblins, dwarfs,</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Child: </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">you were taken to be the son and sometimes the apprentice of your Keeper. Your Durance forced you into growing up, same as with the other Lost, but you managed to not turn into a bitter adult and remained a Child at heart. No matter what aspect of childhood predominates inside you, your blessing is &quot;Endless Curiosity&quot;: you gain a +3 to all Perception and Research rolls.</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Fairest Child: The Peter Pan. Darkling Child: Tom Swayer. Ogre Child: The Gentle Giant Or The Bully. Elemental Child: One With Nature. Beast Child: <a href=\"http://&#91;/SIZE\" target=\"_blank\">The Calvin</a>. Wizened Child: The Savant.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-24-2015, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T01:31:04-07:00","id":492435,"title":"","content":"I like the Royal Kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T02:53:26-07:00","id":492472,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see a Kith that deals with Oneiromancy... Its one of my fave things from 1e when I'm not having my characters wander the Hedge (to that end I'd love to see more carrot offered for a Changeling to go off the Trods, there was just no reason to proactively do it in 1e, instead it seemed more like a fear tactic to keep on the tracks when in the Hedge, to me at least).<br /> <br /> But yep, I'd really like to see what a Keeper may have as a Kith to place on their changeling that helps them in the dreamscape... Especially with potential links to Beast:the Primordial now too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}